<figure id="S2.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S2.T2.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>. </span><span id="S2.T2.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comprehensive comparison of ranking performance (<span id="S2.T2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">nDCG@10</span>) on BEIR datasets across three ICR-based settings: all-layer aggregation (<span id="S2.T2.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">All</span>), selective interval aggregation (<span id="S2.T2.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Selective</span>, <math id="S2.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[l_{1}\!-\!l_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.072em">−</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[l_{1}\!-\!l_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>), and single peak-layer aggregation (<span id="S2.T2.9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Peak</span>, <math id="S2.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{l\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mi>l</mi><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{l\}</annotation></semantics></math>). The best result within each model triad is highlighted in <span id="S2.T2.9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>.</span></figcaption>
